# 16 Find Correlation of the student study hours vs score
cor(student_performance$study_hours_per_day,
    student_performance$overall_score)

# The correlation between study hours and overall score is -0.0036, which is very close 
# to zero this indicate that there is no meaningful relationship between study hours and the student performance
# Study quality is not equal to study hours

# 17 Find correlation in between Attendance vs Score 
cor(student_performance$attendance_percentage,
    student_performance$overall_score,
    use = "complete.obs")

# The correlation between attendance and overall score is 0.1487 indicating a weak positive 
# relationship this suggest that while higher attendance may slightly improve performance it is not
# strong factor influencing student scores

# 18 What relationships can be observed between study hours, attendance, sleep, and 
# overall score using a pair plot

ggpairs(student_performance[, c("study_hours_per_day",
                 "attendance_percentage",
                 "sleep_hours",
                 "overall_score")])

# The pair plot shows that study hours have the strongest positive relationship with overall score, while sleep hours have the weakest.
# A pair plot was used to examine the relationships among study hours, attendance, sleep hours, and overall score. The scatter plots indicate a positive
# relationship between study hours and overall score, suggesting that students who study more tend to achieve higher scores. Attendance percentage also shows
# a moderate positive relationship with performance. However, sleep hours appear to have a weaker relationship with overall score, as the data points are more scattered.

